  "strategy": "Approach and Rationale:\nThe central idea is to represent the function h(x) as a packed sequence of exponentially-damped triangular steps. This representation is motivated by the observation that good solutions for the minimum overlap problem often feature broad, shallow features rather than sharp peaks. The method systematically explores a lower-dimensional parameterization of the full n-point solution space, enabling efficient optimization. We use a particle-spring-mass analogy where features represent masses connected by springs (representing correlations), and optimize this system to minimize overlap. This parameterization significantly reduces the dimensionality, allowing deeper explorations within the time budget.\n\nMaterials:\n- Mathematical formulation showing equivalence to minimizing the overlap integral\n- Dimensionality reduction from n points to \u223clog n parameters\n- Rigorous justification in the implementation details\n- Focus on the exponential decay parameter (\u03c4) which captures feature broadening\n\nKey Limitations:\n1. Smoothness deficit: The representation has limited ability to capture sharp features (natural for minimum overlap)\n2. Gevrey class: Normalization may miss discontinuities (low risk for overlap minimization)\n\nMathematical Specification:\n1. Representation:\n   h(x) = \u2211_{k=1}^{m} a_k * \u03c8_\u03c4(x - b_k)\n   \u03c8_\u03c4(x) = exp(-|x|/\u03c4) / (1 + |x|/\u03c4)   [window function]\n\n2. CVXPY Formulation for Projection:\n   minimize ||y - y_observed||^2_2\n   subject to 0 \u2264 y \u2264 1, \n              \u03bb_n <= \u222b y dx <= \u039b_N,\n              \u2211 \u03c8_\u03c4 scaling parameters = \u03b7\n\nImplementation Procedure:\n1. Parent Validation:\n   a. Validate initial_h_values in native resolution\n   b. Project to feasible form using minimum projection error under TV norm\n\n2. Core Update Loop:\n   a. Initialize m=8 steps with \u03c4=logscale\n   b. For each optimization stage:\n      i. Sample \u03c4 from pre-defined lognormal distribution\n      b. Use trimmed L-BFGS-B solver with active constraints\n      iii. Add convergence trails (dither + slosh)\n\n3. Candidate Acceptance:\n   a. Accept new point if |\u0394C| < 0.0 or improvement > 1e-4\n   b. Use shadow function with \u03b5=0.03 for local minima detection\n\n4. Hyperparameter Search:\n   a. \u03bb_\u03b5 = 0.1, \u03b1=0.85 (annealing)\n   b. Decay schedule: \u03c4_new = \u03c4_old^(1-\u03b2) with \u03b2=0.98\n\n5. Search Choices:\n   Initial: \u03c4_min=0.2, \u03c4_max=5.0 (dB scale)\n   Toggles: Smoothing iterations based on min(feature_count, 16)\n   Deviation: 30% from current error rate\n\n6. Budget Allocation:\n   Stage1: 300s (global \u03c4 scan, 30 trials)\n   Stage2: 600s (gradient polishing, adaptive)\n   Stage3: 200s (downsampled resolution, 180 points)\n   Rest: Error evaluation\n\nSearch Choices and Variations\nInitial Configuration:\n\u03c4_center = median last-stage error, \u03c3 = error^0.5 (variance)\nLocal Search: 0.75*C change from localslide\nGlobal Renormalization: biweekly with \u03b1=0.95\n\nKey Variations:\n1. Wing factor oscillation: \u03c4_wing \u2208 {0.5, 1.0, 2.0} (0.05*\u03c4_step)\n2. Wavelet subsampling: power=2.0 (Fourier subtraction)\n3. F. Jumps with N_max=6 per dimension\n4. Mode selection (greedy vs wholebatch)\n\nComputational Budget and Robustness\nDim-aware timing: log n operations for n-point validation\nDeadline polling: After each successful move (1e-6*dim time)\nFallback: Clamped solution with inverted step counts\n\nValidation and Return Contract\nFinal checks:\n- \u222bh dx = \u03b7\u00b11e-9 (\u03b7=n/2 scaling)\n- Use explicit gradient checking for random subset (dim/2 or \u03b5)\n- Default sanity checks: h in [0,1] with max(correlation) < C (parent+0.0)\n- Epsilon insertion: Testing against polarities for erratic solutions\n\nImplementation Details:\nh = [w_i * exp(-(x-center_i)/\u03c4) / (1 + |x-center_i|/\u03c4) for all_points]\n\nParameters: \n  \u03c4_scales = [-0.4, -0.1, 0.0, 0.2, 0.5, 1.0, 1.8]  (base deviations)\n  \u03b7 = current_grid_sum / target_sum (adjustment)\n  proj_error = ||sum(h)-\u03b7||_inf (if >1e-3, fail)\n\nGradient Projection:\nUse sparse matrix representation for force vectors,\nSupport derivative: d\u03c8/d\u03c4 = exp(-|x|/\u03c4)/\u03c4 * |x|/\u03c4 * (\u03c8 derivative w.r. time)\n\nStop Conditions:\n- User-defined: \n  improvement < 1e-9 across 4e3 evaluations\n  counted \u03c4 space exploration < aggressive limit\n  manual_swattch > 30% of CPU capacity\n\nErd\u0151s-Specific Checks:\n- Verify overlap formula matches existing correlation.calculate(dx)\n- Use l1projection (not clipping) for uncertainty principle\n- Normalize across lags with analytic interpolation (not nearest)\n- Trust C_regional = min(max(shifted correlation), 0.38)",
